    {
      "title": "Measurements and reference values",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Positive findings on cannabis in PD come from open-label or uncontrolled designs that the sources treat with caution: a 2026 single-center open-label prospective cohort of 68 patients initiating medical cannabis reported improvements in the Non-Motor Symptoms Scale total score at 3 months, with a dropout rate of 26.5%, and its authors call the findings exploratory; an earlier systematic review states that positive effects described in uncontrolled studies have not been confirmed by the few and small RCTs; and the Parkinson's Foundation consensus statement says studies suggesting non-motor benefit are generally small, uncontrolled and open label, and that more rigorous research is needed. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42304702/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:01dda4605dfb10f7d0158ef47a12f0f92d138eb9a9124c4ad18bd04131b7449f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
