          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the CBD-PD-BRH trial (Parkinsonism & Related Disorders, volume 135, June 2025), sixty PD patients were randomized to sublingual CBD or placebo and 51 were analysed; the authors report that the primary outcome, MoCA delayed recall, showed no group differences, that the CBD group improved naming scores (mean difference 0.37, 95 % CI 0.01 to 0.73) at a mean CBD dose of 26 mg/day, and that alkaline phosphatase was elevated in the CBD group with no serious side effects in either group. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1353802025005826",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:919d81eb9b49b98086bb308e0a8f47a77dc5d9df9d5e568b15c4acb018a91bd2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
