            "ev:da82fb2baac38ff08a290095fa85ee863c82ee55132d3f25fd90a77cf79d66c2",
            "ev:dd039278285e8e6a5727670b06c0c9114dbb2789736e40e628670268a53841be",
            "ev:ee6d4357393f87c8fa5698f6e2f06adc1e3ac89e3528481ef5a523eee8b0eaae"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In an exploratory double-blind trial of 21 PD patients without dementia or comorbid psychiatric conditions (placebo, CBD 75 mg/day or CBD 300 mg/day; seven per group), Chagas et al. found no statistically significant differences in UPDRS scores, plasma BDNF levels or H(1)-MRS measures, while mean total PDQ-39 scores differed between the placebo and CBD 300 mg/day groups (p = 0.05); the authors write that their findings point to a possible effect of CBD in improving quality of life measures and that studies with larger samples and specific objectives are required before definitive conclusions can be drawn. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25237116/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9881f86343dd955abb0ba77f27a8c0fd6a7403458dcbc75f1a9409b923ab3954",
