    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In the Colorado phase 2 randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of oral CBD/THC in PD (61 randomized: 31 CBD/THC, 30 placebo; final dose of 2.5mg/kg/day), motor MDS-UPDRS was reduced by 4.57 with CBD/THC and 2.77 with placebo and the between-group difference was not significant (-1.80, p = 0.379); the registry record NCT03582137, which gives the same enrollment window (9/5/2018 to 1/4/2022) and the same 61 randomized, posts a net mean difference of -1.8049 and p = 0.3785; the authors report that sleep, cognition and activities of daily living showed a treatment effect favoring placebo, and conclude that the brief duration and strong placebo response limit interpretation but there was no benefit, perhaps worsened cognition and sleep, and many mild adverse events. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11102313/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5a3c20604fa662707ef902041076fa4cd2c56f48ccf7a892bf5d4723dec2c01e",
