          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As published, the Parkinson's Foundation consensus statement (May 2020) says that, given the lack of any clear data supporting the use of cannabis in PD, the Foundation does not endorse its use for PD symptoms or to modify disease progression; the Foundation's web page states that there is no conclusive evidence marijuana helps with PD symptoms; and a document hosted on the Michael J. Fox Foundation website, with content current to March 2022, states that controlled trials have not yet proven the safety or benefit of cannabis in Parkinson's. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/sites/default/files/documents/medical_cannabis_statement_finalv2_5.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:562ebfce2e39bb38e3b22bd6e6c3d51faaee4d8d5e10f37dd3102d94fcc25c3e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
