        {
          "text": "The 2014 American Academy of Neurology systematic review of medical marijuana in selected neurologic disorders concluded that oral cannabis extract is probably ineffective for treating levodopa-induced dyskinesias in patients with Parkinson disease; the PubMed record title of this report carries the label [RETIRED], and the Parkinson's Foundation 2020 statement cites the same AAN conclusion. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
